# 10. OFFICIAL CHALLENGE #11 — AUTOMATIC POST-DISCHARGE FOLLOW-UP

This is the MOST IMPORTANT workflow for hackathon alignment.

Build a fully functional post-discharge task management system.

## HOSPITAL WORKFLOW

When hospital staff select:

**"Bemorni uyga chiqarish"**

Open a form containing:

- Patient
- Hospital
- Treating doctor
- Discharge timestamp
- Relevant discharge instructions
- Patient's district
- Assigned territorial family doctor
- Follow-up priority defined by authorized clinical staff
- First follow-up deadline

## AUTOMATIC TASK CREATION

When discharge is confirmed:

1. Save the discharge event.
2. Create a post-discharge monitoring case.
3. Identify the responsible family doctor from authorized organization mappings.
4. Create a follow-up task.
5. Set deadline to discharge timestamp + 24 hours.
6. Notify the assigned family doctor.
7. Log the action in the audit timeline.
8. Display the task in the family doctor's dashboard.

If a doctor cannot be identified:

- Set status to "Biriktirilmagan".
- Place the task in an administrative assignment queue.
- Notify authorized coordination staff.
- Do not invent an assigned doctor.

## FOLLOW-UP TASK STATUS

Use states:

- Yangi
- Qabul qilindi
- Jarayonda
- Bajarildi
- Muddati o‘tgan
- Qayta biriktirish kerak

## FAMILY DOCTOR ACTIONS

The doctor can:

- Accept task
- View relevant patient details
- Record patient contact
- Record contact method
- Add follow-up notes
- Request further review
- Complete the follow-up

The doctor's actual follow-up must be recorded.

An AI call or SMS does not count as physician completion.

## DEADLINE TRACKING

Display a live 24-hour countdown.

If the deadline passes without completed physician follow-up:

- Mark the task as overdue.
- Notify authorized supervisors.
- Keep the task visible until resolved.

Use persistent server timestamps.

Do not depend solely on an open browser tab.

## PRIVATE CLINIC WORKFLOW

Also support a separate workflow:

"Post-Procedure Follow-Up"

Example:

A dentist treats a patient and schedules follow-up check-ins.

The treating dentist can monitor that patient directly.

This private clinic workflow is separate from the official hospital-to-territorial-family-doctor workflow.

