# 23. SECURITY, PRIVACY AND HEALTHCARE SAFETY

This is a healthcare product.

Security and safety are essential.

## MANDATORY RULES

- Separate demo data from real user data.
- Do not use actual patient records in the MVP demo.
- Require secure authentication for real user accounts.
- Implement backend authorization.
- Apply organization-level isolation.
- Limit access to authorized clinicians.
- Maintain audit logs for sensitive record actions.
- Do not expose API keys to frontend code.
- Do not place health data into public URLs.
- Avoid displaying private medical details in generic SMS previews.
- Validate all user inputs.
- Prevent unauthorized role changes.
- Protect clinician notes and patient contact information.
- Design explicit consent controls for AI phone calls.
- Allow consent withdrawal.
- Do not send actual calls or messages to unconsenting people.
- Treat AI summaries as drafts requiring professional review.
- Never present the prototype as clinically validated.
- Never claim official government integration without authorization.

Provide reasonable security defaults.

Prepare the app for future compliance review, but do not claim that building this MVP automatically makes it compliant with healthcare regulations.

